WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nice to see you.
-Nice to see you.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so cool to be
in this building, man.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to say, this is, like,
a big deal for me.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a big "SNL" junkie.
-Fantastic.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.507 line:92%
Well, this is the place to be.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have to ask you a question.
-Go for it.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.845
-So, Will Ferrell was hosting
this weekend, as you know.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I was reminded of a sketch
that for "SNL" fans

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
is sort of hallowed ground
for just, like,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best stupid sketch
of all-time.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
I recently watched it,
and I realized, oh, my God,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
a young Seth Meyers
is right in the front row,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I want to know
if you have the same affection

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
for Gus Chiggins
and the old prospector.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.262 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Old prospector, yeah.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.197
-As I do, and many other people.
-Yes.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just to know
what that was like.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.534 line:92%
-Well, it was -- I tell you,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they just put it
on YouTube.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was my third week
at the show.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:38.772 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's amazing.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was a really emotional
week at the show

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.110
because someone had sent anthrax
to the building.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:49.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
So everybody -- It was like
right af-- it was 2001.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:49.916 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So it was a crazy time.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was so --
That sketch was so dumb.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it nose-dives down
the rabbit hole really easy.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:59.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Will makes choices
that no other performer --

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.226 line:92%
and he does that all the time --

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he makes --
he takes so many pauses.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:05.065
-Oh, you could see, all of you
guys are like, what is going on?

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:05.832 line:92%
-Yeah, I had this moment of

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.901
"Oh, my God, if I laugh,
they're going to fire me,"

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.170
and then I look around at, like,
Jimmy Fallon, and Horatio.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Well, they're still
here, so I'm fine."

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.207
-But in that moment, do you know
that it's, like,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is something people
are going to like

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.078
or are you like, "Oh, my God."
-The crazy thing was it got cut.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was only at dress,
so that was the thing is

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought, "Oh, this is
the greatest thing

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.015 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that ever happened."

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:25.218
And then I thought, "Oh, great
things get cut all the time.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:25.885 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm just new here."

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.288
And then they really don't.
-That was it. That was the one.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Most things that get cut
are like,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.291
"Yeah, that was the right thing
to get cut."

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.827
-If you don't know it, go check
out the old prospector.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Old prospector, now available
on YouTube.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Delightfully stupid.
It's amazing.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.766
-We, actually -- So, we ran
into each other backstage

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.467 size:78% position:39% line:92%
at the Golden Globes.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.801
-Yeah.
You did a great job by the way.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
But I was --

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.504 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.974 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We had -- Thank you.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:48.908 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We had an after party,

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
and someone told me
you were on your way.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
I left because
my wife was pregnant.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.447 size:84% position:42%
But you did make it in,
but it was not easy.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.584
-Oh I could not get into your
party, no, no, they don't.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.751 line:92%
-But you were on the list.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.953 line:92%
-Yeah, that's what they tell me.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would have been nice
at the time.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.956 line:92%
No, we got in eventually.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact my fiancée and I,
we took a guy that we met --

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.893 line:92%
we thought we were being nice,

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
being like,
"Dude, we're on the list.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.829 line:92%
We'll take you to the party."

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Okay,
let me get the Uber."

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:12.832 line:92%
So we're, like, riding high,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "We'll show this guy
a good time.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.702 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We're Hollywood folks."

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we get there
and they're like, "No."

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then go figure,
this guy goes,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.275 size:84% position:42%
"Hey, I know that guy,"
and he walked us in.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, really?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.777
-Always takes the guy you think
isn't allowed at the party.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.746 size:84% position:42%
-Did you give him money
for the Uber I hope?

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.783
-No, no, I took that free ride.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.485 line:92%
-So, we were talking backstage.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
First two episodes of the show
is fantastic.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play not a serial killer,
I guess. What --

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess the terminology
is spree killer.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not
a licensed criminologist,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.696 line:92%
but it's a little different.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Andrew Cunanan,
who killed Gianni Versace

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
and four other men
in the course of a very --

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:52.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it like getting in
the head of someone like that?

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you the kind of actor
who does that,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
or are you just kind of --
-Yes and no.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.477 line:92%
I mean, look, I'm an actor.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you obviously have to act
the part, so to speak,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.582
but as far as putting your head
in that space,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think people tend to forget
that people's lives

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.655
are much greater than the worst
things they've ever done.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:12.125
And while obviously what he did
is deplorable and horrible

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:15.461
and still has echoes of tragedy
20 years later, I --

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.563 line:92%
This is a bizarre comparison.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:21.267
But if you -- like if I met you
at a bar on a bad night for you.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:21.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.070
-And then I told all my friends,
Seth Meyers is a jerk.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even though that's really just
one night of your life.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.509
-I think the most I ever killed
in one night was three.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was three, and that's like,
who's counting?

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's a bizarre comparison.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I'm saying is
we all have --

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to kind of count
the primary colors

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.652 line:92%
between you and another person.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't approach it as,
"Oh, this guy killed people."

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you also play him
because he was --

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:49.495
I mean, a liar, fabulous about
his own life to some degree.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you have to bring a lot of
charm and charisma

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.967
to this character who obviously
we are seeing --

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're kind of
zoned into this awful time.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:58.771
-Yeah, he was a famously likable
guy most early in his life.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.906 line:92%
When I was saying we don't know

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody from the worst things
ever done.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
I met so many people that met
him throughout his life

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
that really were
quite fond of him,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.547 line:92%
and he was famously affable.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.314 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Somebody came up to me.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in Vegas.
I was at a concert.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.719
This guy comes up to me, he was
like, "You have to meet my wife.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
She went to high school
with Andrew."

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:15.688 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And she came up to me,

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's talking about,
like, a teenage --

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:18.958 line:92%
like a 15, 16-year-old kid.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.528
She's like, "I just want to let
you know that when I met Andrew,

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.696 line:92%
he was such a good friend to me.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.899
He was somebody you could count
on, and I was heartbroken."

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's when you go, "Okay,
we're not playing --

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:33.172
We're playing a person who has
gone down this destructive path,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how does something so
promising

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.909 line:92%
become something so horrible?"

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:37.844 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That's kind of where --

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you do a fantastic job
with it.

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.348
I can't wait to see the rest of
it because I --

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.651
you know, it's not one of those
shows where you tune in,

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're like,
"Oh, that's a psycho killer."

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do a great job of bringing
a lot of the layers to it.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:50.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you for having me.
This is so cool.

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.027
-I'm so glad you didn't have
trouble at the door tonight.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and they let me
in this time.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.530 line:92%
-Darren Criss, everybody.

